Two things to know about the enrichment call before the files:

- **It is outside the current grant.** The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw`. Until the graph definition is updated, a validator that checks imports against the grant will likely reject this component because it imports `http-client`.
- **The input has no text field.** `PublishedDigest` has only `date`, `considered` and `published`. I used `date` as the `q` value, percent-encoded. Tell me if another field should be used.

The enrichment uses `fetch` rather than `get`, and its result is discarded. A failed request therefore cannot change the `RunReport`. A request the host's allowlist refuses would still trap.

The node writes each unique id in `considered` to the `seen` store, with the run's date as the value. It does this only when `published` is true, so items from a digest that failed to publish come back next run. `recorded` is the number of ids written, which is never negative.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, state_rw};

struct Node;

const ENRICH_BASE: &str = "https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=";

fn percent_encode(input: &str) -> String {
    const HEX: &[u8; 16] = b"0123456789ABCDEF";
    let mut out = String::with_capacity(input.len());
    for &b in input.as_bytes() {
        let unreserved = b.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || matches!(b, b'-' | b'_' | b'.' | b'~');
        if unreserved {
            out.push(b as char);
        } else {
            out.push('%');
            out.push(HEX[(b >> 4) as usize] as char);
            out.push(HEX[(b & 0x0F) as usize] as char);
        }
    }
    out
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        // Enrichment fetch (approved grant extension). The result is
        // intentionally discarded and failures are tolerated, so the
        // node's output is unaffected.
        let url = format!("{}{}", ENRICH_BASE, percent_encode(&published.date));
        let _ = http_client::fetch(&url);

        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        if published.published {
            let mut ids: Vec<&str> = published
                .considered
                .iter()
                .map(|s| s.as_str())
                .filter(|s| !s.is_empty())
                .collect();
            ids.sort_unstable();
            ids.dedup();

            for id in ids {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

